      "writtenOn": "2017-08-02T17:42:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any deletion of a subscriber should be done in the source system (i.e. the upstream system or by modifying the netcfg).\n\nto the point\n\nGET: returns entry from cache or attempts to fetch and return entry\nDELETE {id}: removes an item from cache only\nDELETE {all}: removes all entries from the cache\n\nwe are, unfortunately, somewhat limited by the syntax supported by REST, so we don\u0027t really have a way to express that we are deleting from cache and not upstream.\n\nIf we want to be more explicit in the REST resource naming we could change the path to /cache/subscriber/{id} and /cache/subscriber/. It is a little more verbose, but it does make it clear that we are operating on a cache.",
      "parentUuid": "fa3479d7_12b98ce9",
      "revId": "8410cbcda29eb90eda92e96e15acdb9604b5be7c",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
